{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"wishful-spidersilk-bellsnake","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nChange 3039 (merged 3beb7e4ad23, story fuchsia-wettish-leafbird) made `signature_findings` in `src/rebar/_engine_support/validate.py` classify the op-cert verdicts `invalid` and `key_not_valid_at_era` as MAJOR `[SIGNATURE]` findings alongside `mismatch`. The LLM-Review advisory on that change noted that no test drives a real op-cert record through `signature_findings` to either verdict, so the new classification is unpinned.\n\n## Approach\nAdd tests that write a real op-cert SIGNATURE event, corrupt it so `verify_opcert_record` returns `invalid` (e.g. a malformed or tampered envelope), and separately produce `key_not_valid_at_era` if the verifier can reach it from a store fixture; assert `signature_findings` returns exactly one MAJOR finding naming the ticket. If `key_not_valid_at_era` is unreachable from the op-cert verify path, record that finding on this ticket and drop it from the mapping instead of keeping dead classification.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A test asserts an `invalid` op-cert yields one MAJOR `[SIGNATURE]` finding from `signature_findings`.\n- [ ] `key_not_valid_at_era` is either pinned by a test the same way or removed from the mapping with the reason recorded here.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","id":"5a7a-9aa9-73e4-4125","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["test-gap"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Test signature_findings maps a real op-cert's invalid / key_not_valid_at_era verdicts to MAJOR findings"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1792373321172628521,"uuid":"24fa03f1-d128-43b9-8534-54496e07edea"}